(What is RAG?) Tj
0 -19 Td
/F1 11 Tf
(Retrieval-Augmented Generation \(RAG\) is a technique that gives a large language) Tj
0 -17 Td
/F1 11 Tf
(model relevant information from external documents before it answers. Instead of) Tj
0 -17 Td
/F1 11 Tf
(relying only on what it learned during training, the model reads retrieved text) Tj
0 -17 Td
/F1 11 Tf
(and uses it as context. RAG was introduced by Patrick Lewis and colleagues at) Tj
0 -17 Td
/F1 11 Tf
(Facebook AI Research in a 2020 paper.) Tj
0 -17 Td
/F1 11 Tf
() Tj
0 -17 Td
/F1 13 Tf
(The three stages of RAG) Tj
0 -19 Td
/F1 11 Tf
(1. Indexing: documents are split into chunks, each chunk is converted into an) Tj
0 -17 Td
/F1 11 Tf
(   embedding vector, and the vectors are stored in a vector index such as FAISS.) Tj
0 -17 Td
/F1 11 Tf
(2. Retrieval: the user question is embedded with the same model and the most) Tj
0 -17 Td
/F1 11 Tf
(   similar chunks are found using similarity search.) Tj
0 -17 Td
/F1 11 Tf
(3. Generation: the retrieved chunks are added to the prompt and the LLM writes) Tj
0 -17 Td
/F1 11 Tf
(   an answer grounded in that context.) Tj
0 -17 Td
/F1 11 Tf
() Tj
0 -17 Td
/F1 13 Tf
(Why use RAG?) Tj
0 -19 Td
/F1 11 Tf
(RAG lets a model answer questions about private or recent documents without) Tj
0 -17 Td
/F1 11 Tf
(retraining, reduces hallucinations, and makes it possible to show the sources) Tj
0 -17 Td
/F1 11 Tf
(that an answer was based on.) Tj
0 -17 Td
/F1 11 Tf
() Tj
0 -17 Td
/F1 13 Tf
(What is FAISS?) Tj
0 -19 Td
/F1 11 Tf
(FAISS \(Facebook AI Similarity Search\) is an open-source library developed by Meta) Tj
0 -17 Td
/F1 11 Tf
(for efficient similarity search over dense vectors. An IndexFlatIP index compares) Tj
0 -17 Td
/F1 11 Tf
(a query vector with every stored vector using the inner product.) Tj
0 -17 Td
